# Keeps the repository-root build context small. Both images build from the root
# (backend/Dockerfile needs docs/, which is a sibling of backend/; Dockerfile.fly
# needs frontend/ and packs/), and without this file the context would include a
# ~200 MB virtualenv and a ~80 MB node_modules that neither image uses — both
# reinstall their dependencies inside the image.
#
# Nothing listed here is COPYed by either Dockerfile. Check before adding a line.
.git
.github
**/node_modules
**/.venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
frontend/dist
# Secrets never belong in an image layer; compose passes them as environment.
.env
